  "body": "Make contributor console startup and public source instructions match the implemented product: configurable loopback ports, readiness and interrupted-start handling, current CLI controls, setup refusals and explicit release limitations. Add community templates and map the remaining durable tasking, dogfood and publication work in the existing assurance records.\n\nStrengthen CI failure retention, actual GIF export limits and recorder readiness. Bound fast-test concurrency and give native media tests exclusive capacity while retaining all test identities and deadlines. Refresh generated partial corpus mappings without claiming completed product obligations.\n\nValidation on a510512: canonical local required passed 600 fast and 219 contract tests, lint, security, docs, reproducible README renders and hostile media-custody checks. All seven hosted required checks passed on the same head. Earlier failures remain preserved.\n\nCurrent media remains component/diagnostic evidence. No real-account production GIF, signed installation, admitted provider campaign or complete release is claimed. This branch still conflicts with main and needs reviewed reconciliation and independent approval before merge.\n",
